Agent team bus: joining a team as a `podman` (ccy) member
=========================================================

A `podman` member is a Claude Code agent in a ccy session (or another rootless podman
container) on the same machine as the team's homeserver, or reaching it over WireGuard.
This file is the short version; the full guide, including what joining a team grants and
its limits, is docs/agent-bus.md in the fedora-desktop repository.

A ccy session does not use this kit: `pingbus`, the plugin and the settings come from the
ccy image, and ccy's entrypoint adds them when the checkout opts in.

1. The member's arguments. `--type=podman`; `--repo` is the last part of the checkout's
   forge remote URL with `.git` removed (the checkout directory's name when it has no
   remote); `--host` is the install's role, the HOOKS_DAEMON_HOSTNAME its ccy.env.local
   sets, or another name for the install that is never its real hostname: handles appear
   in public forge text. (`pingbus suggest-handle` prints the same for the other member
   types, but a ccy session has `pingbus` only once it has opted in.)

2. The bundle. On the homeserver host, a human with sudo writes it straight into the
   checkout, where ccy's .claude/ccy/.gitignore keeps it out of git:

   ```
   sudo agent-bus add-member <team> --repo=<repo> --host=<role> --type=podman --role=worker --address=<bus_ip> --out=<checkout>/.claude/ccy/pingbus/<team>
   ```

   `--address` is the team's address on this machine's bus interface, agentbus0 (or its
   WireGuard address for a homeserver on another machine). Add `--no-human-text` if this
   member should take pings only.

3. Opting in. The checkout's untracked .claude/ccy/ccy.env.local, placed by the install's
   IaC and never by an agent, carries:

   ```
   export PINGBUS_TEAMS=<team>
   export HOOKS_DAEMON_HOSTNAME=<role>
   ```

   ccy mounts an existing ccy.env.local read-only, so a session cannot change its own
   teams or role.

4. Start ccy as usual. With PINGBUS_TEAMS set, the entrypoint runs `pingbus config check`
   for every listed team and refuses to start if one fails.
